- Firebase local `.env`: ignored by Git.

## Consumption SKU and cost preflight (2026-11-01)

### Availability evidence

- The user's registered-provider metadata lists `Australia East` for `Microsoft.App/managedEnvironments`.
- The user's `Microsoft.App` quota and usage responses report the applicable `ManagedEnvironmentCount` limit as 1 and usage as 0 (0/1).
- The user ran `az containerapp env workload-profile list-supported --location australiaeast --output table`; the result lists `Consumption` alongside `D4`, `D8`, `D16`, `D32`, `E4`, `E8`, `E16`, `E32`, `Flex`, and GPU profile types. This confirms regional Consumption profile availability in the user's authenticated Azure CLI context.
- The deployment availability tools still reject this subscription ID, so SKU/region details are grounded in the user-provided authenticated CLI evidence rather than those tools.
- Azure's Container Apps billing documentation distinguishes Consumption (per-resource, scale-to-zero) from Dedicated (provisioned workload profile). This design must stay on Consumption and avoid dedicated profiles, private endpoints, and planned maintenance.

### Retail-price estimate

Standard USD retail rates returned for `australiaeast`:

| Component | Rate / included usage | Estimated monthly effect |
|---|---|---|
| ACR Basic registry unit | USD 0.1666/day | About USD 5.00 per 30-day month, before any storage/network overages |
| ACA Consumption active vCPU | USD 0.000034 per vCPU-second | Billed after the subscription's monthly free grant |
| ACA Consumption active memory | USD 0.000004 per GiB-second | Billed after the subscription's monthly free grant |
| ACA Consumption requests | USD 0.40 per million requests | First 2 million requests per subscription/month are free |
| ACA Consumption grants | 180,000 vCPU-seconds and 360,000 GiB-seconds per subscription/month | Approximately 100 active hours at 0.5 vCPU + 1 GiB, if the grants are unused |
| Azure Static Web Apps Free | Free plan | USD 0 while within Free-tier limits |
| Log Analytics | First 5 GB/month free at billing-account scope | USD 0 only while the shared free grant is not exceeded |

For a planning scenario of one 0.5-vCPU/1-GiB replica with `minReplicas=0`, `maxReplicas=1`, no other ACA grant usage, no more than 2 million requests, logs within the shared 5-GB free grant, and no billable egress:

- ACA compute is approximately USD 0 through the first 100 replica-active hours/month.
- Above that, active compute is approximately USD 0.0756 per replica-hour before remaining free grants; ACR plus ACA is about USD 8.78 at 150 active hours/month.
- The USD 10 Azure-only budget is reached at roughly 166 active hours/month under these assumptions. A continuously active 730-hour month would be approximately USD 52.63 (ACR plus ACA after the free grants), before log, network, tax, or currency effects.
- If another workload consumes the free grants, the estimate changes: 150 active hours would cost about USD 16.34 for ACA plus Basic ACR, exceeding the cap.

The user confirmed the planning assumptions of 0-100 replica-active hours/month, at most 2 million requests, logs at or below 5 GB/month, and an Azure-only USD 10/month cap. Under this specific planning scenario, estimated Azure spend is approximately USD 5/month (ACR Basic; ACA within the currently unused grants; SWA Free; logs and requests within shared free grants). This is within the Azure-only cap with about USD 5 nominal headroom, but is not an account-specific quote. The ACA size remains a planning assumption; the Bicep requires operator-selected CPU, memory, and replica limits. Gemini API and Qdrant Cloud charges are explicitly outside this Azure-only budget.

The Azure Retail Prices API reports an `Environment Management Hour` meter at USD 0.10/hour effective 2026-11-01. The Azure Container Apps billing documentation ties management charges to features such as private endpoints and planned maintenance; neither is in the intended staging design. Do not enable either without a new cost review.

Sources: [Azure Container Apps billing](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/billing), [Container Apps retail prices in Australia East](https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?$filter=serviceName%20eq%20%27Azure%20Container%20Apps%27%20and%20armRegionName%20eq%20%27australiaeast%27&currencyCode=USD), [Container Registry retail prices in Australia East](https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?$filter=serviceName%20eq%20%27Container%20Registry%27%20and%20armRegionName%20eq%20%27australiaeast%27%20and%20skuName%20eq%20%27Basic%27%20and%20meterName%20eq%20%27Basic%20Registry%20Unit%27&currencyCode=USD), [Static Web Apps pricing](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/app-service/static/), [Azure Monitor pricing](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/monitor/).

## Blockers before a deployment plan can be finalized

1. The user confirmed the filtered inventory is empty; no Resource Group, ACA, ACR, SWA, or Log Analytics resource was found.
2. The user verified the subscription is `Azure for Students` and the selected ID matches the supplied subscription. However, the deployment availability and quota tools still report that this subscription is invalid or inaccessible to those tools.
3. In the user's Azure CLI context, `Microsoft.App`, `Microsoft.Web`, `Microsoft.ContainerRegistry`, `Microsoft.OperationalInsights`, and `Microsoft.Quota` are registered. ACA managed-environment quota is 0/1 and the user confirmed the Consumption profile is listed for Australia East.
4. User-provided location metadata lists `Australia East` for `Microsoft.App/managedEnvironments` and `Microsoft.ContainerRegistry/registries`, but not for `Microsoft.Web/staticSites`; SWA's listed regions are Central US, East US 2, West US 2, West Europe, and East Asia. The user approved East Asia for SWA.
5. Bootstrap Bicep compiles locally. The cloud `what-if` is blocked until the tenant's Azure MFA requirement is met; both ordinary and device-code `az login` completed but did not satisfy the policy. Stop repeated retries and ask the tenant administrator to verify MFA registration/claims for Azure Resource Manager. The existing `infra/aca/staging.bicep` remains a candidate-revision module for later releases.
6. Azure-only estimated cost is approximately USD 5/month under the user's stated low-use assumptions. This is not a guaranteed total cost and excludes Gemini/Qdrant and any usage exceeding shared free grants.
7. The Qdrant Cloud cluster exists, but the three staging collections are not created. Qdrant API key is not available to the deployment process.
8. Confirm whether the existing Firebase project may be shared with staging or whether staging needs a separate Firebase project.
9. CI/CD platform has not been selected. Do not create a pipeline until the user chooses GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps, or another platform.

